{"shortDescription":"Custodian Property Income REIT plc (CREI)Custodian Property Income REIT plc: Share Buyback24-Sep-2026 / 10:02 GMT/BST24 September 2026Custodian Property Income REIT plc(“Custodian Property Income REIT” or the “Company”)Share BuybackCustodian Property Income REIT (LSE: CREI), which seeks to deliver…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Custodian Property Income REIT plc (CREI)"]},{"type":"p","children":["Custodian Property Income REIT plc: Share Buyback"]},{"type":"p","children":["24-Sep-2026 / 10:02 GMT/BST"]},{"type":"p","children":["24 September 2026"]},{"type":"p","children":["Custodian Property Income REIT plc"]},{"type":"p","children":["(“Custodian Property Income REIT” or the “Company”)"]},{"type":"p","children":["Share Buyback"]},{"type":"p","children":["Custodian Property Income REIT (LSE: CREI), which seeks to deliver a strong income return by investing in a diversified portfolio of smaller regional properties across the UK, announces that yesterday it purchased 100,000 ordinary shares of 1 pence each in the capital of the Company (“the Shares”)."]},{"type":"p","children":["The Shares were acquired for consideration of £81,000 (plus costs and expenses) at a cost per share of 81.0 pence, representing a 17.8% discount to dividend-adjusted net asset value, and will be held in treasury. This transaction was executed under the irrevocable, non-discretionary share buyback programme (“the Programme”) announced on 17 July 2025 and extended on 11 June 2026 which instructs Deutsche Bank AG to operate the Programme independently during closed periods."]},{"type":"p","children":["Following this transaction, the Company holds 6,895,732 of its ordinary shares in treasury and has 488,217,079 ordinary shares in issue (excluding treasury shares)."]},{"type":"p","children":["- Ends -"]},{"type":"p","children":["Further information:"]},{"type":"p","children":["Further information regarding the Compa